  "worked_solution": "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\u2207\\times (f\\,F)=f\u2207\\times F+\u2207f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\u2207f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2z \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z) & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-2z(y)]i-[0(0)-2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z)]j+[0(y)-0\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z)]k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i+2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z)j+0\\,k \\\\  & =\u27e8-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z),0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\times (f\\,F) & =f\u2207\\times F+\u2207f\\times F \\\\  & =(1+{z}^{2})\u27e80,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x+z),0\u27e9+\u27e8-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z),0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x+z),0\u27e9+\u27e8-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z),0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2yz,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x+z)+2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+z),0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\times (f\\,F)(\\pi ,1,0) & =\u27e8-2(1)(0),(1+(0)^{2})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi +0)+2(0)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi +0),0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,-1,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
